Fix file URI formatting and path relocation on Windows

1. On Windows, absolute file paths start with drive letters (e.g. C:/...).
   Prepending 'file://' results in 'file://C:/...' with two slashes instead of
   three (RFC 8089). libxml2 / xsltproc treats 'C:' as the network authority /
   host, failing with:
     xsl:import : invalid URI reference file://C:/...
   Ensure proper 3-slash 'file:///' URIs and safe encoding.

2. Resolve DATADIR and XSL stylesheet paths relative to the script location
   when configured paths are not directly accessible, enabling full relocatability
   without hardcoding build-time prefixes.

3. In mal-ncx.xsl and mal-opf.xsl, use relative stylesheet includes to yelp-xsl
   so stylesheets resolve cleanly regardless of install root.

